
  ▲ vercel teams switch [name]

  Switch to a different team                                                    

  Global Options:

       --cwd <DIR>            Sets the current working directory for a single   
                              run of a command                                  
  -d,  --debug                Debug mode (default off)                          
  -Q,  --global-config <DIR>  Path to the global `.vercel` directory            
  -h,  --help                 Output usage information                          
  -A,  --local-config <FILE>  Path to the local `vercel.json` file              
       --no-color             No color mode (default off)                       
       --non-interactive      Run without interactive prompts; when an agent is 
                              detected this is the default                      
  -S,  --scope                Set a custom scope                                
  -v,  --version              Output the version number                         


  Examples:

  - Switch to a team. If your team's url is 'vercel.com/name', then 'name' is the slug. If the slug is omitted, you can choose interactively

    $ vercel teams switch <slug>

  Notes:

  Saves the team in the global config, so later commands use it until you switch
  again. --scope overrides it for one command.                                  

  In a directory linked to a project, commands keep using the project's team.   

  A scope is always a team: there is no personal account to switch to.          

  Related:

  vercel teams list  Show all teams that you're a member of                   
  vercel whoami      Shows the username of the currently logged in user.      


